    "body": "Originally posted as \r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/45346475/skype-bot-unable-to-join-group-chats-was-able-to-before\r\n\r\n## System Information (Required)\r\n* SDK Language: ReST API\r\n* SDK Version: -\r\n* Development Environment: LOCALHOST, AZURE_BOT_SERVICE\r\n\r\n## Issue Description\r\nI have a skype bot which was working fine and was able to join and interact in Group Calls Now (July 27th) it seems to have stopped working\r\n\r\nIf I try to add the bot to a Group Call I get the initial callback. But my Answer Action does not seem to get the subsequent callback from the Skype Channel. Note: The call is successfully joined if it's only 1:1, not a Group Call.\r\n\r\nI have Group Messaging \"on\". (Since it was working earlier) I have tried this on our Production Bot, QA Bot, and even a bot for my local development. All Group Calls have ceased on all (different) bots. I have tried calling the Bot 1:1, successfully, and then adding somebody to the conversation. This also does not work as the third person is unable to join the call (no reason specified).\r\n\r\nHas this functionality been removed entirely?\r\n\r\n## Steps to Reproduce the Issue\r\n1. Create a group call on a skype client\r\n2. Add Bot\r\n3. Bot does not answer\r\n\r\n## Expected Behavior\r\nAnswer Action should lead to the webhook being called. Hence letting the Bot answer the call.\r\n\r\n## Actual Results\r\nNo webhook callback initiated after responding with a Answer Action\r\n(Only in a group call)\r\n",
